# The executables that link a C library, and so are built natively for each architecture inside the userland of the
# build userland, Ubuntu 22.04, whose glibc (2.35) is older than that of Ubuntu 26.04 and Rocky 10 and whose symbols stay at
# GLIBC_2.34 or below, the glibc of Amazon Linux 2023 (ADR 0013, "One version"; docs/runtimes/bare-metal.md, "Supported
# operating systems"). 22.04 is the build userland, not a supported board image.
# `just build-arm64` leaves them to this build (it cross-compiles with CGO off), and picks up their output.
#
# Columns, separated by a tab: the package below the repository root, and the Go build tags.
drivers/key/yubikey-piv	sluis_card
